# FIDE Service — sample gateway hardening (LiteSpeed/cPanel Apache syntax).
#
# HUMAN ACTION REQUIRED. This file is DOCUMENTATION, not live config:
# review it, adapt hostnames/paths, and install the resulting rules into
# the production .htaccess (alongside the existing SetEnv secrets, which
# must NEVER be committed). Nothing here is applied by deploying the repo.
#
# Split of responsibilities with the Flask app (interfaces/factory.py):
#   app sets:     X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy (works everywhere)
#   gateway sets: HTTP->HTTPS redirect, HSTS (only the TLS terminator can
#                 do these correctly). X-Frame-Options/CSP are omitted on
#                 purpose: this service renders no HTML for browsers.
#
# <IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
# RewriteEngine On
# # API must never be served over plain HTTP (MITM swaps, credential
# # sniffing). Probes should target https:// directly.
# RewriteCond %{HTTPS} !=on
# RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://%{HTTP_HOST}%{REQUEST_URI} [R=301,L]
# </IfModule>
#
# <IfModule mod_headers.c>
#   # HSTS: only valid over HTTPS; max-age one year. includeSubDomains
#   # affects every subdomain of the API host — remove it if other
#   # subdomains are not fully HTTPS-ready.
#   Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
#   # Belt-and-braces duplicates of the application headers (harmless):
#   Header always set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
#   Header always set Referrer-Policy "no-referrer"
# </IfModule>
#
# Rate limiting note (audit M2): per-IP/per-key global caps cannot be
# expressed in .htaccess on this stack. They belong at the server or CDN
# layer (LiteSpeed server-level throttle rules, or a proxy such as
# Cloudflare Rate Limiting) as a separate human action. The in-app
# per-key + pre-auth per-IP limiters (interfaces/api/auth.py) remain as
# defense-in-depth regardless.
